{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-roadtypes-runspec",
    "description": "PENDING (PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, §7.3.43). The `expand-roadtypes` RunSpec -- Washtenaw, August, weekday 6am, passenger cars on four fuels, Total Energy Consumption at running and start exhaust -- on ALL FIVE road types: off-network 1 beside on-network 2, 3, 4 and 5. 729 rows = running exhaust on five road types x 125 cohorts + start exhaust on road type 1 x 104. It does NOT reproduce. It is the first RunSpec in the corpus with more than one on-network road type, and the first with an on-network process (running exhaust) and road type 1 in the same run, and the model computes neither: `run_selectionUnported` is 4 here and 0 on every document in `runspecs/`.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON, MEASURED 2026-10-20 against the snapshot rather than guessed. Two pieces, and the first is an axis.\n\n* THE ROAD TYPE AS AN AXIS. `run_roadTypeID` is one number per run (`run_rows`): the activity relation has no road-type axis, so a running-exhaust rate is computed on exactly one road type. Here it sums the four on-network selections to 14, joins no `Link` row, and every emitted row comes back at county 0 with emissionQuant 0. The forward closure of `run_roadTypeID` in `onroad/model.esm` is 284 of its 1517 variables, one equation each: 153 already county-shaped, 68 that are not -- the drive-cycle operating-mode stack (`lomd_*` 31, `asb_*` 8, `asd_*` 4, `dsa_*` 4, `pp_W*` 5, over `drive_second_rows` x `physicsrow_rows`), the activity VMT and speed (`act_*`, `run_roadTypeVMTFraction`) and the output ordinals (`rt_`, `pcoh_`, `spc_`) -- and 63 per-run, per-pollutant-process and output variables whose road type becomes per block. 119 of the 284 reach it ONLY through the run's geography ids (`run_linkID`, `run_zoneID`, `run_countyID`, `run_stateID`, `run_linkRoadTypeID`) -- the tank-temperature, tank-fuel and hotelling stacks among them (`ttg_` 23, `tfg_` 15, `hot_` 12) -- and need no axis if the zone and state are found by county alone; the other 165 carry the road type genuinely. The road-type-independent part is real: the road-4 block of this run equals the Washtenaw block of `expand-counties` cell for cell, all 125, and sums to 240.727491 as `expand-counties-large`'s does.\n\n* OFF-NETWORK IDLE (ONI), A NEW MECHANISM. Running exhaust on road type 1 is 125 rows summing to 31.31, against 240.73 on road type 4, and it is `TotalActivityGenerator` step 190c (`moves.rs` `generators/totalactivitygenerator/allocation.rs` `off_network_idle_sho`): per age, SHO(1) = max(S x (TIF - sum(SHO_r x DIF_r)/S) / (1 - TIF), 0), S the SHO summed over the zone's on-network links, DIF_r `BaseRateGenerator`'s driving-idle fraction per road type (the SHO-free idle share of each road's drive-cycle operating-mode distribution: 0.00505, 0.05721, 0.03030 and 0.12842 for 2..5 here) and TIF `totalIdleFraction` at the state's idle region (Michigan, 103 Midwest), the county's `countyTypeID` (1), the month, the day type and the model year -- 0.245044679. The formula reproduces the snapshot's age-0 SHO on link 2616101, 188.612, from the four on-network SHO values. Its rate is the idle mode alone: `BaseRateGenerator` writes road type 1 running exhaust as opMode 1 at fraction 1, avgSpeedBin 0 and an average bin speed of 1 mph (`baserategenerator/drivecycle.rs`), so the snapshot's `baserate_1_2020` carries 125 rows on each of road types 1 through 5. The default database ships `totalIdleFraction`, `State.idleRegionID` and `County.countyTypeID`; the model ingests none of them yet. Whether ONI sums the zone's on-network SHO over the SELECTED road types or over all four is not decidable from this snapshot, which selects all four.\n\nTHE SHAPE CHECK MOVES WITH THEM. The output relation gains a road-type level and is ragged across it -- start exhaust on one road type, running on five -- so `tools/check-runspec-shape.py`'s `rows == rateSurvivorCount x counties x months x day types` needs the (pollutant-process, road type) block rather than the pollutant-process as its leading factor, and `run_offNetworkLinkCount`, which licenses evaporative `SourceHours = SHO`, would count this run's road-type-1 link (it reads 0 today only because the link join fails) and has to stop counting a run whose road type 1 carries no evaporative process.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 729, what the run emits, not to what the chain computes (104 start rows, every one at county 0 and 0 g): the document validates and is not evaluated, and the binding is the number the finished model has to recompute.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-roadtypes",
      "pending"
    ]
  },
